# Raging River with Isshin, Two Heavens as One: a lone attacker - Memnite, exactly the "one or more" - triggers the River
# twice (CR 603.2d), and each resolution makes its own piles and label, each restriction holding on its own. Bot2
# puts Phyrexian Walker and Crookshank Kobolds "left" the first time, Kobolds of Kher Keep and Crookshank Kobolds "left" the
# second; Memnite is labelled "left" both times. Only Crookshank Kobolds, "left" in both, may block it: Phyrexian Walker and
# Kobolds of Kher Keep are each "left" in only one resolution's piles, which says nothing of the other's: the Walker would
# block only if the second label read the first resolution's piles, the Kher Keep only if the first read the second's.
[Bot1 Deck]
Raging River
Isshin, Two Heavens as One
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Memnite
Mountain
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Phyrexian Walker
Kobolds of Kher Keep
Crookshank Kobolds
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Raging River.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Isshin, Two Heavens as One.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Phyrexian Walker.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Kobolds of Kher Keep.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Crookshank Kobolds.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
Bot2.Choose(Phyrexian Walker; Crookshank Kobolds)
Bot1.Choose(Memnite)
Bot2.Choose(Kobolds of Kher Keep; Crookshank Kobolds)
Bot1.Choose(Memnite)
Bot2.Pass
! Bot2.Block(Phyrexian Walker > Memnite)
! Bot2.Block(Kobolds of Kher Keep > Memnite)
Bot2.Block(Crookshank Kobolds > Memnite)
? Combat.Blocks = Crookshank Kobolds > Memnite

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Phyrexian Walker.BlockRestriction = In the "left" pile; In the "right" pile
Bot2.Battlefield.Kobolds of Kher Keep.BlockRestriction = In the "left" pile; In the "right" pile
Bot2.Battlefield.Crookshank Kobolds.BlockRestriction = In the "left" pile; In the "left" pile
